course: dictionary
lesson: 12192
title: Finding a confidant in a story
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A confidant is a person you trust enough to tell your secrets and private feelings. You can find the meaning by reading the words around it. «Priya told Ruby about her secret plan, because Ruby was her confidant.» Priya shares a secret with Ruby, so Ruby must be someone Priya trusts.
explain: Look at what the character does with that person. «Sam told Mr Hughes he felt worried, and every week they talked after school.» Sam shares private feelings with Mr Hughes, so Mr Hughes is Sam's confidant. Ask yourself: who does the character tell their secrets to? That person is the confidant.
explain: A confidant can be a friend, a grandparent or a teacher. «Dad was the only confidant she trusted with her secret.» Here the word shows that Dad is the one person she can trust completely. A trusted friend means much the same thing, so you can swap the words and check the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A confidant is a person you trust with your secrets and private feelings.
fact: A confidant can be a friend, a grandparent or a teacher.
fact: «Confidant» is used for a man or a person of any gender; «confidante» is the feminine form.
fact: A trusted adult is someone you can talk to when you have a worry.
fact: A good check is to swap in «trusted friend» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Ella told only her big sister about the lost kitten, so her sister was her confidant.» What is a confidant? | A stranger on the bus | A shop worker who sells sweets | A teacher who gives out homework | *A person you trust with your secrets
exercise: «Grandad listens to all of Ravi's worries, and Ravi tells him everything. Grandad is Ravi's confidant.» Which phrase means the same as confidant? | *Trusted friend | Stranger | Enemy | Neighbour
exercise: Which sentence shows a confidant? | The bus was late again. | *Maya whispered her secret to Chloe, her closest friend and confidant. | The shop sold apples and pears. | Tom ran around the park.
test: In «Mr Okafor had been Jamal's confidant for years, so Jamal told him about the move.», what kind of person is Mr Okafor? | A person Jamal has only just met | *A person Jamal trusts with secrets and private feelings | A person who sells newspapers | A person who fixes cars
test: Which word is the feminine form of confidant? | confidence | conflict | *confidante | confided
exam: Which best describes a confidant? | A stranger you met today | A loud shout | Someone who tells everyone your news | *A person you trust to keep your secrets
